   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "scm_step60_surface_soil",
     "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay_physics=1 sf_surface_physics=1 (slab, num_soil_layers=5) bl_pbl_physics=1, data/eqwefic/scm_ref), step 60 (20:00 UTC = 13:34 LST, gsw = 315 W/m^2, rnet = 237 W/m^2, hfx = 71 and lh = 199 W/m^2, G = -32.6 W/m^2 into the soil). Inputs: the phy_prep state entering surface_driver from the driver-level dump subassembly_pbl (fork 592f693) plus the surface-layer option flags and previous-step exchange quantities from the kernel-level sfclayrev dump of the same step, and the land-use thermal inertia THC, radiation/ifsnow flags and the fixed deep soil layer from the kernel-level slab dump. References: surface-layer outputs from the sfclayrev kernel dump (real32, rel 2e-5 -- the measured 4e-6 floor of the component times 5); slab outputs from the real64 slab_driver replay of the same step at ESM_DT = 0.01 s (the exact instantaneous derivative, slab tests), rel 2e-5 on the radiative terms and hfx, 5e-5 on the moisture terms (real32 svpt0 amplified by the saturation deficit), 1e-4 on G_sfc and hm (small differences of large terms), 1e-3 on dTsk_dt and Linf abs 1e-7 K/s on the soil-layer tendency column; land and capg exact. The WRF finite-step skin change (tsk_out - tsk)/dt = 9.0e-5 K/s is asserted against the instantaneous 1.003e-4 K/s with rel 0.15 only to document the 11 %% sub-stepping gap (FORTRAN_BUGS N12), not as a physics test.",
